  "_comment": "Shared vectors for the payload hash a signed station change carries (svitgrid D-2204): payloadSha256 is the lowercase hex SHA-256 of the payload's canonical JSON (keys sorted at every level, no whitespace, numbers as JavaScript prints them, an absent payload as {}). The API builds the payload and hands it to the phone, the phone signs that hash, and the board recomputes it from the payload it receives. Read by services/api/src/__tests__/signing/canonical-json.test.ts, apps/mobile/test/core/signing/station_command_event_builder_test.dart and devices/edge-connector-v2/test/test_canonical_json.c; the add-on keeps a copy in tests/fixtures. Regenerate canonical and sha256 only from the TypeScript encoder, and never edit them by hand.",
